1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,072
He was a dentist in Hagen, and he became one of the most

2
00:00:03,072 --> 00:00:06,510
highly decorated panzer commanders of the Wehrmacht.

3
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:09,160
His name was Franz Bäke.

4
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:12,803
In the First World War he fought as a young volunteer,

5
00:00:12,803 --> 00:00:16,600
then he studied dentistry and opened a practice.

6
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:21,760
In August 1939, at 41, he was called up.

7
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:25,632
With the 6th Panzer Division he fought in Poland, in France

8
00:00:25,632 --> 00:00:29,330
and on the Eastern Front, before Stalingrad and at Kursk.

9
00:00:29,380 --> 00:00:34,890
By the end of 1943 the dentist was leading an entire panzer regiment.

10
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:40,350
In early 1944 the Wehrmacht formed a special unit for him:

11
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:47,830
around 34 Tigers and 46 Panthers under one command, Heavy Panzer Regiment Bäke.

12
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:54,110
In February 1944 it was to free the troops trapped in the Cherkassy pocket.

13
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:57,470
But a thaw turned the roads into mud, and the tanks

14
00:00:57,470 --> 00:01:01,330
got stuck about 20 kilometres short of the pocket.

15
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:03,880
Bäke received the Swords to the Knight's Cross,

16
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:06,690
the 49th soldier of the Wehrmacht to do so.

17
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:10,650
In April 1945 he became a major general.

18
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:14,710
And after the war he did something hardly any general did.

19
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:19,140
He went back to Hagen and worked as a dentist again.
